<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1463" root="اوب" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْبَةٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْبَةٌ</span></b>  <i>Return;</i> (T, A, K;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِيَابَةٌ</span></b> , a subst. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آبَ</span>. (Msb.) You say,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِيَهْنِئْكَ أَوْبَةُ الغَائِبِ</span> [<i>May the return of the absent
give thee joy</i>]. (TA.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلانٌ سَرِيعُ الأَوْبَةِ</span> and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَيْبَةِ</span></b>  <i>Such a one is quick in return.</i> (A 'Obeyd,
T, S. *) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>Return from disobedience to obedience;
repentance.</i> (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايب</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلَامٌ لَا أَوْبَةَ لَهُ</span>
<i>Speech,</i> or <i>language, without profit.</i> (A.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْبَةٌ</span> is also the sing. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْبَاتٌ</span>, which signifies The
<i>legs</i> of a beast. (K, TA.)

